# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/dagger.clip: the dagger family (P2c ACTIONS-1H, wave 2; STYLE_P2 12, 25.8). Generated by
# ACTIONS-1H's gen1h.py: the drawn idle / walk / run (the sword's loco lines with this family's guard), hit 1-3 (windup,
# strike, follow + the recover in the guard; hit 3 holds its impact), and the shield bearer's lines (`when shield`).
# (wave-2 fix round 2, ACTIONS; C3d) hit 2's windup facing R cocks the blade back at the hip (dg_3w, a135 behind): on
# dg_2w the fist and the blade both went behind the body (no hand pixel); a shield bearer's hit 2 facing D stabs on hit 1's
# arms (dg_1s, dg_1f) with hit 2's lean: dg_2's cross-body stab put the fist under the shield.
# (wave-2 fix round 3, ACTIONS; C3d) a shield bearer facing L (the dagger in the far fist) blocks and winds hit 1 up with
# the dagger cocked back at the hip, the blade up behind the body (dg_3w, a045 behind): on dg_1w a180 the far fist sat
# behind the torso and the blade under the shield, so neither read (72 lines, every T5 shield bearer).
# (wave-2 fix round 4, ACTIONS; C3d) a shield bearer facing U keeps the dagger fist wholly clear of a cape: the block holds
# the dagger at the guard (oh_g) while the shield takes the blow, hit 1's windup rides the dagger's raised arm (dg_3w), its
# follow the strike arm (dg_1s) (dg_1w / dg_1f showed two hand pixels past the cape's edge, the grip under it: 10 lines);
# hit 2's windup facing L cocks the blade level behind the head (a000: at a023 its point stood a pixel clear of the helm, D90).

